rules.content:
#### 规则概述
`no-async-promise-executor` 规则旨在防止在 Promise 构造函数的执行器函数中使用 `async` 关键字。

##### 规则意义
使用 `async` 关键字会导致 Promise 执行器的行为不符合预期，因为它会返回一个新的 Promise，而不是预计中的值。这可能会导致难以追踪的错误或意外行为。

##### 错误示例
```javascript
const myPromise = new Promise(async (resolve, reject) => {
    // 这里使用了async
    const result = await someAsyncFunction();
    resolve(result);
});
```

##### 正确示例
```javascript
const myPromise = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    // 这里没有使用async
    someAsyncFunction().then(resolve).catch(reject);
});
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
The `no-async-promise-executor` rule aims to prevent the use of the `async` keyword in the executor function of a Promise constructor.

##### Rule Meaning
Using the `async` keyword causes the behavior of the Promise executor to be unexpected, as it returns a new Promise instead of the intended value. This can lead to hard-to-trace errors or unintended behavior.

##### Error Example
```javascript
const myPromise = new Promise(async (resolve, reject) => {
    // async is used here
    const result = await someAsyncFunction();
    resolve(result);
});
```

##### Correct Example
```javascript
const myPromise = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    // async is not used here
    someAsyncFunction().then(resolve).catch(reject);
});
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在循环中使用 `await` 可能会导致性能问题，因为这将导致循环中的每一次迭代都必须等待前一次的异步操作完成。

##### 规则意义
当在循环中使用 `await` 时，可能会导致不必要的延迟，降低代码执行效率。为了提高性能，建议使用并发方法处理多个异步操作。

##### 错误示例
```javascript
async function processItems(items) {
    for (const item of items) {
        await doSomethingAsync(item); // 在循环中使用 await
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```javascript
async function processItems(items) {
    const promises = items.map(item => doSomethingAsync(item)); // 使用 map 收集所有的 promise
    await Promise.all(promises); // 并发执行
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Using `await` in a loop can lead to performance issues, as it causes each iteration in the loop to wait for the previous asynchronous operation to complete.

##### Rule Meaning
When using `await` in a loop, it can introduce unnecessary delays, reducing the efficiency of code execution. To improve performance, it is recommended to handle multiple asynchronous operations concurrently.

##### Incorrect Example
```javascript
async function processItems(items) {
    for (const item of items) {
        await doSomethingAsync(item); // Using await in a loop
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```javascript
async function processItems(items) {
    const promises = items.map(item => doSomethingAsync(item)); // Collecting all promises using map
    await Promise.all(promises); // Executing concurrently
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
本规则禁止在代码中使用位操作符。

##### 规则意义
位操作符（如 `&`, `|`, `^`, `<<`, `>>` 等）在JavaScript中并不常用，且可能造成代码可读性差和不易维护。建议使用更直观的代替方案，例如逻辑操作符，以提升代码的可理解性和维护性。

##### 错误示例
```javascript
let a = 5;
let b = 3;
// 错误示例：使用位与操作
let result = a & b;
```

##### 正确示例
```javascript
let a = 5;
let b = 3;
// 正确示例：使用逻辑运算
let result = (a > 0) && (b > 0);
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule prohibits the use of bitwise operators in code.

##### Rule Significance
Bitwise operators (such as `&`, `|`, `^`, `<<`, `>>`, etc.) are not commonly used in JavaScript and can lead to poor code readability and maintainability. It is recommended to use more intuitive alternatives, such as logical operators, to enhance code understanding and maintainability.

##### Incorrect Example
```javascript
let a = 5;
let b = 3;
// Incorrect example: using bitwise AND operator
let result = a & b;
```

##### Correct Example
```javascript
let a = 5;
let b = 3;
// Correct example: using logical operations
let result = (a > 0) && (b > 0);
```

