rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则用于禁止定义具有相同名称的类成员(方法或属性)。若在同一类中定义多个同名成员，可能导致代码可读性下降，并引发潜在的逻辑错误。

##### 规则意义
确保类成员名称的唯一性，可以提高代码的可维护性和可读性，减少潜在的混淆和错误。

##### 错误示例
```javascript
class MyClass {
    method() {}
    method() {}  // 此处重复定义了同名方法
}
```

##### 正确示例
```javascript
class MyClass {
    methodA() {}
    methodB() {}  // 消除了同名方法的定义
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule prohibits the definition of class members (methods or properties) with the same name. Defining multiple members with the same name in the same class can lead to diminished code readability and may cause potential logical errors.

##### Significance of the Rule
Ensuring the uniqueness of class member names can improve code maintainability and readability, while reducing potential confusion and errors.

##### Error Example
```javascript
class MyClass {
    method() {}
    method() {}  // This method is defined multiple times with the same name
}
```

