switch (fruit) {
    case 'apple':
        console.log('Apple');
        break;
    case 'banana':
        console.log('Banana');
        break;
    case 'orange':
        console.log('Orange');
        break;
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule prohibits the definition of duplicate case labels in switch statements.

##### Rule Significance
Using the same case label in a switch statement can lead to confusing code logic and may result in erroneous program behavior, creating code that is difficult to maintain.

##### Incorrect Example
'''javascript
switch (fruit) {
    case 'apple':
        console.log('Apple');
        break;
    case 'banana':
        console.log('Banana');
        break;
