rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is designed to prohibit the use of specific syntax structures to improve code consistency and maintainability.

##### Rule Importance
By restricting certain syntax, potential issues or structures that may be difficult to understand can be avoided in the code. This helps the team maintain simplicity and consistency in the code during development.

##### Incorrect Example
```javascript
for (let i = 0; i < array.length; i++) {
    console.log(array[i]);
}
```

##### Correct Example
