array.forEach(item => {
    console.log(item);
});
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则检查代码中是否存在自我比较的情况，即变量与自身进行比较。

##### 规则意义
自我比较通常是代码逻辑中的一个错误，可能导致意外的行为或难以理解的代码。通过检测此类比较，可以提高代码的可读性和可靠性。

##### 错误示例
```javascript
if (a === a) {
    console.log('这段代码有问题');
}
```

##### 正确示例
```javascript
if (a === b) {
    console.log('这是有效的比较');
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks for the presence of self-comparison in the code, that is, a variable being compared to itself.

##### Rule Meaning
Self-comparison is generally an error in the logic of the code, which may lead to unexpected behavior or code that is difficult to understand. By detecting such comparisons, the readability and reliability of the code can be improved.

##### Error Example
```javascript
if (a === a) {
    console.log('这段代码有问题');
}
```

##### Correct Example
```javascript
if (a === b) {
    console.log('这是有效的比较');
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则旨在禁止在 setter 方法中返回一个值。在JavaScript中，setter 应该仅用于设置对象属性，而不应返回任何结果。

##### 规则意义
在 setter 中返回一个值会导致混淆和不必要的副作用，这可能会影响到程序的可读性和可维护性。开发者在使用 setter 时通常会预期它们不返回任何值，因此应避免这种做法。

##### 错误示例
```javascript
class Example {
    set value(val) {
        return val;
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```javascript
class Example {
    set value(val) {
        this._value = val;
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to prohibit returning a value in setter methods. In JavaScript, setters should only be used to set object properties and should not return any results.

##### Rule Significance
Returning a value in a setter can lead to confusion and unnecessary side effects, which may impact the readability and maintainability of the program. Developers typically expect setters not to return any value, so this practice should be avoided.

##### Incorrect Example
```javascript
class Example {
    set value(val) {
        return val;
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```javascript
class Example {
    set value(val) {
