rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则用于检测变量名冲突的问题，也就是在嵌套的作用域中，外层作用域的变量与内层作用域的变量同名，这可能会导致代码的可读性和可维护性降低。

##### 规则意义
避免变量名冲突能够增强代码的可读性和降低潜在的错误。尤其是在复杂的函数或块中，清晰的变量名能够让开发人员更容易地理解代码的意图，防止潜在的逻辑错误。

##### 错误示例
```javascript
function example() {
    var x = 'outer';
    function inner() {
        var x = 'inner'; // 这里与外层的x同名，造成冲突
        console.log(x);
    }
    inner();
    console.log(x);
}
``` 

##### 正确示例
```javascript
function example() {
    var outerX = 'outer';
    function inner() {
        var innerX = 'inner'; // 使用不同的变量名，避免冲突
        console.log(innerX);
    }
    inner();
    console.log(outerX);
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect variable name conflicts, specifically when a variable in an outer scope has the same name as a variable in an inner scope. This can lead to decreased readability and maintainability of the code.

##### Rule Significance
Avoiding variable name conflicts can enhance code readability and reduce potential errors. Especially in complex functions or blocks, clear variable names can help developers better understand the intent of the code and prevent potential logical errors.

##### Incorrect Example
```javascript
function example() {
    var x = 'outer';
    function inner() {
        var x = 'inner'; // This conflicts with the outer x by having the same name
        console.log(x);
    }
    inner();
    console.log(x);
}
``` 

##### Correct Example
```javascript
function example() {
    var outerX = 'outer';
    function inner() {
        var innerX = 'inner'; // Using different variable names to avoid conflicts
        console.log(innerX);
    }
    inner();
    console.log(outerX);
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则禁止使用三元运算符，提倡使用更可读的条件语句。

##### 规则意义
三元运算符虽然简洁，但在复杂的逻辑中可能导致代码可读性下降。使用常规的`if`语句可以使代码结构更加清晰，便于后续维护。

##### 错误示例
```javascript
const result = condition ? '条件成立' : '条件不成立';
```

##### 正确示例
```javascript
let result;
if (condition) {
