rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在子类构造函数中，`this` 必须在调用 `super()` 之前访问，否则会导致运行时错误。

##### 规则意义
这是JavaScript类的构造函数的一条基本规则，确保在子类构造函数中正确初始化父类，以避免潜在的错误。未遵循此规则将导致代码在运行时抛出异常。

##### 错误示例
```javascript
class Parent {
    constructor() {
        this.value = 42;
    }
}
class Child extends Parent {
    constructor() {
        console.log(this.value); // 错误，this 在 super() 之前访问
        super();
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```javascript
class Parent {
    constructor() {
        this.value = 42;
    }
}
class Child extends Parent {
    constructor() {
        super(); // 正确，首先调用 super()
        console.log(this.value); // 现在可以安全地访问 this
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In a subclass constructor, `this` must not be accessed before calling `super()`, otherwise it will lead to a runtime error.

##### Rule Significance
This is a fundamental rule of JavaScript class constructors, ensuring the proper initialization of the parent class in the subclass constructor to avoid potential errors. Failing to adhere to this rule will result in an exception being thrown at runtime.

##### Error Example
```javascript
class Parent {
    constructor() {
        this.value = 42;
    }
}
class Child extends Parent {
    constructor() {
        console.log(this.value); // Error, this is accessed before super()
        super();
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```javascript
class Parent {
    constructor() {
        this.value = 42;
    }
}
class Child extends Parent {
    constructor() {
        super(); // Correct, call super() first
        console.log(this.value); // Now it is safe to access this
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
