rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则旨在防止在循环条件中使用可能被修改的变量，这可能会导致意想不到的行为和无限循环。

##### 规则意义
在循环中，如果条件是一个可以在循环体内被修改的变量，将导致该循环的行为不易预测。此规则提醒开发者注意这一点，以提高代码的可维护性和防止潜在的无限循环问题。

##### 错误示例
```javascript
let i = 0;
while (i < 10) {
    // i在此可能被修改
    console.log(i);
    if (someCondition) {
        i++;
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```javascript
let i = 0;
const max = 10;
while (i < max) {
    console.log(i);
    i++;
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to prevent the use of variables in loop conditions that may be modified, which can lead to unexpected behaviors and infinite loops.

##### Rule Significance
In a loop, if the condition is a variable that can be modified within the loop body, it will lead to unpredictable behavior of that loop. This rule serves as a reminder for developers to be aware of this issue to improve code maintainability and prevent potential infinite loop problems.

##### Incorrect Example
```javascript
let i = 0;
while (i < 10) {
    // i may be modified here
    console.log(i);
    if (someCondition) {
        i++;
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```javascript
let i = 0;
const max = 10;
while (i < max) {
    console.log(i);
    i++;
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则用于检测代码中存在的不可达代码。这是指在执行过程中不会被执行的代码，比如在函数的某个分支中返回后，后续的代码将不会被执行。

##### 规则意义
不可达代码通常是一个潜在的缺陷，可能会导致代码维护困难、逻辑混乱或性能下降。它们应该被移除，以提升代码的可读性和执行效率。

##### 错误示例
```javascript
function example() {
    return true;
    console.log('This will never be executed'); // 不可达代码
}
```

##### 正确示例
```javascript
function example() {
    console.log('This gets executed');
    return true;
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect unreachable code present in the codebase. Unreachable code refers to code that will not be executed during the execution process, such as code that comes after a return statement in a branch of a function.

##### Rule Significance
Unreachable code is often a potential defect that can lead to difficulties in code maintenance, logical confusion, or performance degradation. It should be removed to enhance code readability and execution efficiency.

##### Error Example
```javascript
function example() {
    return true;
    console.log('This will never be executed'); // Unreachable code
}
```

##### Correct Example
```javascript
function example() {
    console.log('This gets executed');
    return true;
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则用于检测代码中存在的不可达循环，确保代码的逻辑可达性。

##### 规则意义
不可达循环会导致性能问题，增加代码的复杂性，并可能导致运行时错误。因此，及时识别和修复这些循环可以提升代码质量和可维护性。

##### 错误示例
