for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    console.log(i);
}

while (condition) {
    // 循环体逻辑
    if (conditionMet) {
        break;
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect unreachable loops in the code, ensuring the logical reachability of the code.

##### Rule Significance
Unreachable loops can lead to performance issues, increase code complexity, and potentially cause runtime errors. Therefore, identifying and fixing these loops in a timely manner can enhance code quality and maintainability.

