rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect unused variables, helping developers identify redundant parts of the code.

##### Rule Importance
Unused variables increase the complexity of the code, reduce its readability and maintainability, and may introduce confusion and errors. By disabling unused variables, code quality and consistency within the team can be improved.

##### Error Example
```javascript
function example() {
    var unusedVariable = 42;
